WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 6.4 · MEAL: Monitoring, Evaluation, Accountability & Learning
Baselines and targets

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
When you are starting out, the starting point is now: capture it before your work begins.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:27.393
A baseline is the value of an indicator before your work starts. A target is the value you aim to reach by a given date. Together they let you show change and judge progress.

4
00:00:27.793 --> 00:00:28.393
Two numbers and the steps between

5
00:00:28.393 --> 00:00:38.981
Baseline: Where things stand at the start, or your plan to find out. For example: Asked at the start: 0 of 4 trainees hold a food-hygiene certificate.

6
00:00:38.981 --> 00:00:49.200
Target: Where you aim to be, and by when. For example: Provisional: 3 of 4 trainees hold the certificate by the end of the six months.

7
00:00:49.200 --> 00:01:00.619
Milestones: Quarterly steps towards an annual target, where that helps you manage. For example: One by month two, two by month four, three by month six.

8
00:01:01.019 --> 00:01:01.619
Why they matter

9
00:01:01.619 --> 00:01:05.811
1. Without a baseline you cannot show change.

10
00:01:05.811 --> 00:01:11.115
2. Without a target you cannot judge whether progress is enough.

11
00:01:11.115 --> 00:01:18.530
3. When you start something new, now is the best moment to capture it.

12
00:01:18.930 --> 00:01:19.530
How you will use them

13
00:01:19.530 --> 00:01:24.463
1. Your monitoring: actual results compared with targets each period.

14
00:01:24.463 --> 00:01:30.137
2. Your evaluation: the baseline is the point you measure change from.

15
00:01:30.137 --> 00:01:36.441
3. Your reports and claims: honest figures with their starting point.

16
00:01:36.841 --> 00:01:37.441
What to avoid

17
00:01:37.441 --> 00:01:42.744
Inventing a baseline: write “to be established by [date]” instead.

18
00:01:42.744 --> 00:01:47.678
Reading too much into a percentage from six people.

19
00:01:47.678 --> 00:01:53.611
Changing targets quietly instead of openly, with a reason.

20
00:01:54.211 --> 00:01:56.011
You set baselines, or plans to establish them, and targets.

21
00:01:56.011 --> 00:02:00.011
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

22
00:02:01.511 --> 00:02:04.611
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
